Error: Jet.RecursiveInlineAlways: `factorial` calls itself, so `#Inline(Always)` cannot expand it
  --> Tests/UI/inline_always_recursive.jet:2:1
    |
  2 | #Inline(Always) factorial: fn(n: Int) -> Int {
    | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Inlining a recursive call would either loop forever at compile time or need an artificial depth cutoff, and neither is a real inline. `#Inline(Always)` guarantees that every direct call is inlined on every tier, or the program is refused: sema refuses a function that calls itself or closes a cycle of marked calls (Jet.RecursiveInlineAlways), one used as a value (Jet.InlineAlwaysAddressTaken), one over the size ceiling (Jet.InlineAlwaysTooLarge), a `#Scrub` routine (Jet.InlineAlwaysScrub), one that reads `context.trace` (Jet.InlineAlwaysReadsTrace) and one with a foreign body (Jet.InlineAlwaysForeign).
 Fix: Drop `#Inline(Always)` (use `#Inline` as a hint), or restructure the function to be non-recursive.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.RecursiveInlineAlways
